          <span class="text-amber-400 transform group-open:rotate-45 transition-transform text-xl">+</span>
        </summary>
        <p class="mt-4 text-gray-400 leading-relaxed">
          Screw pin shackles (e.g. Crosby G-209) use a threaded pin for quick connect/disconnect and are best for temporary, frequently inspected rigging. Bolt type shackles (e.g. Crosby G-2130) use a bolt, nut, and cotter pin that resist vibration loosening, making them suitable for long-term or permanent installations. See the comparison table above.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details class="glass-card p-6 group">
        <summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer list-none">
