          <span class="text-amber-400 transform group-open:rotate-45 transition-transform text-xl">+</span>
        </summary>
        <p class="mt-4 text-gray-400 leading-relaxed">
          Alloy steel shackles (G-209, G-2130) offer higher strength-to-weight ratio and greater impact resistance for critical lifts. Carbon steel shackles (S-209) are an economical choice for general-purpose, non-critical rigging up to 17 tonnes.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details class="glass-card p-6 group">
        <summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer list-none">
          <span class="font-semibold text-white group-hover:text-amber-400 transition">What safety factor do shackles have?</span>
          <span class="text-amber-400 transform group-open:rotate-45 transition-transform text-xl">+</span>
        </summary>
        <p class="mt-4 text-gray-400 leading-relaxed">
          Crosby anchor shackles are designed with a 5:1 safety factor — the minimum breaking load is at least 5 times the WLL. The WLL already includes this factor, so never exceed it regardless of the calculated margin shown in the calculator.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details class="glass-card p-6 group">
        <summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer list-none">
